  "conclusions": {
    "ST-C1": {
      "documentation": "APPROVED",
      "basis": [
        "Legacy directory exclusion precedes list/migration and direct-read selection (IosSnapshotFileSystem152-177,222-228). Initial protection errors propagate rather than entering per-record migration isolation.",
        "Legacy source bytes are deleted only after writeProtected succeeds on the migration path (208-215); current recognized protected records retain their existing precedence/deletion policy (181-189).",
        "Fresh NSURL readback checks the exclusion Boolean (401-418). Apple calls exclusion backup-policy guidance, not an absolute never-in-backup guarantee; doc language correctly avoids a completed-backup/restore claim."
      ],
      "limits": "The existing scoped native approval remains FIXED AND VERIFIED, not real-device backup/restore, physical LAN, Store, or IOS-R1 verification."
    },
    "DS-C01": {
      "documentation": "PRECISION CORRECTION REQUESTED",
      "basis": [
        "Prior preference and marker are read from the persistent application domain, not a resolved fallback. System release restores the prior value or absence only if current singleton exactly matches owned installed value.",
        "Differing external arrays and unmarked old values are preserved; same-value external writes cannot be distinguished from unchanged Parlor-owned preferences.",
        "Persistent marker enables reconciliation by a fresh owner. UserDefaults persistence is asynchronous; no killed-and-relaunched app or guaranteed transaction evidence was produced.",
        "The retained Compose/native controller path does not recreate active sessions merely because language changes."
      ],
      "requested_wording": [
        {
          "location": "docs/PRODUCTION_ARCHITECTURE.md:270-272",
          "change": "Say previous application-domain value or absence. Replace unconditional external preference changes with differing external preference values, ideally mention same-value provenance ambiguity."
        },
        {
          "location": "docs/PRODUCTION_ARCHITECTURE.md:273",
          "change": "Prefer marker is persisted for reconciliation after restart over an unqualified survives restart claim."
        }
      ],
      "limits": "Prior PARTIALLY VERIFIED conclusion is unchanged: unmarked older Parlor override is indistinguishable from legitimate OS per-app preference; same-value external write ambiguity and live restart/UIKit/Compose/device coverage remain explicit."
    },
    "MF-C1": {
      "documentation": "APPROVED WITH SMALL ELIGIBILITY CLARIFICATION RECOMMENDED",
      "basis": [
        "Existing default OFF is retained. Both local and host-only LAN setup submit ConfigureAndStart with chosen settings; reducer validates and installs them atomically only in Setup.",
        "Doctor submits once per night, actor/target must be active and living, and self/repeat restrictions are distinct (reducer279-304). Both UIs apply one Mafia-only predicate after living/active filtering.",
        "ON bypasses only the previous-effective-target restriction, has no fixed streak maximum, and does not authorize second submissions/resurrection. Mafia coordination revote resets only Mafia submissions (519-547).",
        "Skipped night has null effectiveDoctorTarget. Reducer writes that same target into Doctor private previous value and canonical night record (445-475). A Doctor killed that night still protects from the pre-resolution alive set; a later night with no active Doctor resolves null.",
        "Recovery354-365 checks equality with newest retained night record outside PostGame regardless of ON/OFF/death/history cap;478-488 enforces OFF historical consecutive restrictions. Terminal cleanup intentionally clears private previous.",
        "Peer projection omits role map/seed/host-only history while carrying own private data and public settings. Recovery/codec retain the existing serialized flag, with no new migration or game rule introduced.",
        "English and Arabic current switch text describe consecutive nights, not exactly two nights."
      ],
      "recommended_wording": [
        {
          "location": "docs/MAFIA_RULES.md:44-45",
          "change": "Explicit skip clears the consecutive-night restriction for the following night; the target must still be living and otherwise eligible."
        }
      ],
      "limits": "This documentation review adds source-level consistency proof; it does not rerun the prior Mafia test suite, conduct LAN device testing, or approve unrelated Mafia changes."
    }
